   - In 1975 the South American sliver held more people, 41 million against 30 million.
   - Every one of its grids, 2020 included, starts from censuses of about 2010 (2005 to 2012 for the countries on the two slivers), carried backward and forward by growth rates and scaled to the United Nations' country totals of 2022; the grids for 2025 and 2030 use the UN's medium projection.
